EXT. VINEYARD TERRACE - EVENING

Late sun slants across rows of vines. Cicadas. A stone table under a pergola, two glasses of rosé sweating on a linen cloth.

CAMILLE ROUSSEAU-ADEBAYO (30s, linen shirt, bare feet) sits sideways on a bench, one knee drawn up. Opposite her, JOSEPHINE LIND (30s, wide straw hat, sunglasses pushed up into her hair) turns the stem of her glass between two fingers.

Neither has spoken for a long time. The light moves a finger's width across the cloth.

CAMILLE
You're quiet.

JOSEPHINE
I'm looking.

CAMILLE
At what?

JOSEPHINE
At her, the way she sits. I forgot she did that.

CAMILLE
Did what?

Josephine smiles at the vines, not at Camille. A breeze lifts the corner of the cloth and lets it fall.

JOSEPHINE
Nothing.

Camille reaches out and straightens the cloth. Her fingers brush Josephine's, and neither moves them away.

FADE OUT.
